<title>USA: Poland files with U.S. SEC for $300 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Poland files with U.S. SEC for $300 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland filed Tuesday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a registration to sell up to $300 million in notes.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through J.P. Morgan &amp; Co, Merrill Lynch &amp; Co and Salomon Brothers Inc.</p>
<p>The proceeds from the sale of the notes will be used for general governmental purposes, according to the filing.</p>
<p>The notes are not subject to redemption prior to maturity. No other details were available.</p>
</text>
